{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The number of revolutions of a wheel, with fixed center and with an outside diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet, required to cause a point on the rim to go one mile is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db4899686e4e2ec31604c2fe470f7c2ba15ca87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 880 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{440}{\\pi} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{880}{\\pi} \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 440\\pi\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"527\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the radius of the wheel is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> feet, so the total circumference of the wheel is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22af47455fe098ecde8ac2b1ce14710cba3ddc95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\pi$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> feet. We also know that one mile is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/c/2fc92cb8cdff39ca4dac9ec6fb3224dbe5fa50a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5280$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> feet. It takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/8394a878047be03eda32da322f7a61a4d3957b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5280}{6\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" /> revolutions for any one point on the wheel to travel a mile. Simplifying, we find that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a2f9ff83902a0689e15d63379b5f4eaa6c7cfe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } \\frac{880}{\\pi}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"78\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>